+# Tasks
+
+## 1. Repository layer
+
+- [ ] 1.1 Add `CouponRepository.incrementUsedCount(code)` and verify with a focused test that `used_count` increases by one
+- [ ] 1.2 Add `CouponRepository.recordRedemption(orderId, code, discountCents, createdAt)` and verify a row is inserted
+- [ ] 1.3 Add `OrderRepository.applyCoupon(id, discountCents, finalAmountCents, couponCode)` and verify the order row is updated
+- [ ] 1.4 Add a `transaction(db, fn)` helper that commits on success and rolls back on throw, verified by a test that an error leaves data unchanged
+
+## 2. Service business rules
+
+- [ ] 2.1 Implement `OrderService.applyCoupon(id, couponCode)` with request validation (REQ-13) and coupon normalization/lookup (REQ-01) and verify error codes
+- [ ] 2.2 Implement order and coupon checks in precedence order through `COUPON_USAGE_EXHAUSTED` (REQ-02,03,04,10,11) and verify each error code
+- [ ] 2.3 Implement minimum-amount and discount calculation including percent floor and caps (REQ-05..09) and verify boundary values
+- [ ] 2.4 Persist the update, redemption and usage increment in one transaction (REQ-12) and verify rollback on failure
+
+## 3. Route wiring
+
+- [ ] 3.1 Register `POST /orders/:id/apply-coupon` in `src/routes/orders.ts` and verify it returns the updated order shape equal to `GET /orders/:id`
+
+## 4. Tests
+
+- [ ] 4.1 Add tests covering AC-01..AC-05 and AC-10 (discount math, caps, floor, normalization) and verify they pass
+- [ ] 4.2 Add tests covering AC-06..AC-09 (minimum boundary, validity boundaries, repeat application, redemption/usage side effects) and verify they pass
+- [ ] 4.3 Add tests covering every error code and the error-precedence table, verifying no database changes on rejection
+- [ ] 4.4 Run `npm run build` and `npm test` and verify both pass with existing tests unmodified
+
+## Workflow follow-up
+
+- Archive the change once implementation and review are complete.
